00:17:55,975 --> 00:17:58,642
So, I'll, uh... I'll
see you later?

264
00:17:58,677 --> 00:18:00,711
If I'm still here.

265
00:18:04,750 --> 00:18:06,016
Mm.

266
00:18:07,320 --> 00:18:09,297
<i>This won't take long, Dana.</i>

267
00:18:09,321 --> 00:18:14,925
Come on in here...
and tell me about this.

268
00:18:14,961 --> 00:18:17,061
There's no one here but us.

269
00:18:24,203 --> 00:18:26,804
So, you told the police?

270
00:18:26,839 --> 00:18:29,384
I didn't want to
tell them, but...

271
00:18:29,408 --> 00:18:31,008
they questioned me.

272
00:18:31,043 --> 00:18:33,021
That night after you left
Morgan's dressing room,

273
00:18:33,045 --> 00:18:35,112
did you tell anyone
what you'd overheard?

274
00:18:36,215 --> 00:18:38,015
Yeah, I-I shouldn't have.

275
00:18:38,050 --> 00:18:42,319
But I went back to the party,
and I told Don Mosher, and...

276
00:18:42,355 --> 00:18:45,923
and he was standing with
Joey DeFalco and Mr. Anderson.

277
00:18:45,959 --> 00:18:48,092
And you told them about
the blackmail attempt

278
00:18:48,127 --> 00:18:51,295
and that Morgan had gone
back up to her room alone?

279
00:18:51,330 --> 00:18:55,266
I was just so upset; I-I
blurted everything out.

280
00:19:01,106 --> 00:19:03,574
Second runner-up, huh?

281
00:19:03,609 --> 00:19:05,008
Yeah.

282
00:19:05,044 --> 00:19:06,710
It's my best yet.

283
00:19:06,746 --> 00:19:09,046
But now with the
first runner-up dead

284
00:19:09,081 --> 00:19:11,649
and the winner on
trial for the crime...

285
00:19:11,684 --> 00:19:16,053
you could wind up with that
Hollywood contract, couldn't you?

286
00:19:17,489 --> 00:19:20,458
No. I-I didn't kill Morgan.

287
00:19:22,195 --> 00:19:25,362
But there were rumors about her.

288
00:19:25,397 --> 00:19:27,364
What kind of rumors?

289
00:19:27,399 --> 00:19:31,134
Well, like she'd do
anything to win, including...

290
00:19:31,170 --> 00:19:33,504
well, you know, with the judges.

291
00:19:33,539 --> 00:19:35,940
She slept with the judges?

292
00:19:35,975 --> 00:19:37,253
Mm-hmm.

293
00:19:37,277 --> 00:19:40,744
And she was sleeping
with some VIP at the finals.

294
00:19:40,779 --> 00:19:42,992
Well, at least that's
what the rumors were.

295
00:19:43,016 --> 00:19:44,448
I didn't see anyone,

296
00:19:44,483 --> 00:19:46,317
and neither did anyone else.

297
00:19:46,352 --> 00:19:50,087
So maybe the rumors
were just rumors.

298
00:19:54,994 --> 00:19:56,760
Hi, Carl. I'll just be a minute.

299
00:19:56,796 --> 00:19:58,329
Okay. Wait.

300
00:20:00,366 --> 00:20:01,566
Thanks.

301
00:20:05,671 --> 00:20:06,904
Hmm.

302
00:20:09,308 --> 00:20:10,641
Hmm.

303
00:20:13,779 --> 00:20:17,615
Not exactly a natural
beauty, was she?

304
00:20:17,650 --> 00:20:19,183
Oh, hi, Julie.

305
00:20:19,218 --> 00:20:21,785
I thought you'd get
here a lot sooner.

306
00:20:21,820 --> 00:20:23,698
Must've been a long lunch.

307
00:20:23,722 --> 00:20:26,257
Uh... Julie, uh,

308
00:20:26,292 --> 00:20:28,091
let-let me... let me explain.

309
00:20:28,127 --> 00:20:31,428
Uh, Janet and I are just...

310
00:20:31,464 --> 00:20:34,198
two... old friends.

311
00:20:34,233 --> 00:20:36,700
What were you years ago?

312
00:20:36,735 --> 00:20:41,305
Uh, well, just two...
very young friends.

313
00:20:41,340 --> 00:20:42,673
Oh.

314
00:20:42,708 --> 00:20:44,408
Oh, and you've been

315
00:20:44,443 --> 00:20:46,254
thinking about
her all these years.

316
00:20:46,278 --> 00:20:48,311
Oh, no, oh, no, oh, no.

317
00:20:48,347 --> 00:20:51,815
It's just... It's just what?

318
00:20:51,851 --> 00:20:56,854
Well, just, uh...
j... just, you know.

319
00:20:56,889 --> 00:20:58,622
I know what you mean.

320
00:20:58,657 --> 00:21:01,158
Imagine...

321
00:21:01,193 --> 00:21:04,628
well, say, Clay
Ferentol just suddenly...

322
00:21:04,664 --> 00:21:06,697
walked back into my life.

323
00:21:06,732 --> 00:21:08,498
Clay Ferentol?

324
00:21:08,534 --> 00:21:11,134
Mm-hmm. He's the
guy I dated for a while

325
00:21:11,170 --> 00:21:13,270
right after my divorce.

326
00:21:14,607 --> 00:21:16,574
<i>The</i> Clay Ferentol?

327
00:21:16,609 --> 00:21:19,242
That was tight end for
the Dallas Cowboys?

328
00:21:19,278 --> 00:21:20,811
Yes, that's the one.

329
00:21:20,846 --> 00:21:22,980
Anyway, imagine he just
suddenly looked me up

330
00:21:23,015 --> 00:21:25,215
right out of the blue.
You used to date

331
00:21:25,250 --> 00:21:26,917
a pro football player?

332
00:21:26,952 --> 00:21:28,752
Mm-hmm.

333
00:21:28,787 --> 00:21:33,857
So... what if he took
me for long lunches?

334
00:21:33,892 --> 00:21:36,427
How long did you date him?

335
00:21:37,797 --> 00:21:41,198
This isn't going
very well, is it?

336
00:21:41,233 --> 00:21:44,768
Sure it is... I got your point.

337
00:21:44,803 --> 00:21:46,481
Well, uh,

338
00:21:46,505 --> 00:21:48,606
there didn't seem to
be any forced entry.

339
00:21:48,641 --> 00:21:49,885
I noticed that.

340
00:21:54,046 --> 00:21:56,213
Oh, that's, uh, Michelle.

341
00:21:56,248 --> 00:21:59,016
I-I told her... where I'd be.

342
00:22:00,420 --> 00:22:02,319
Hello?

343
00:22:02,354 --> 00:22:03,687
Mm, mm-hmm.

344
00:22:03,722 --> 00:22:05,656
Oh, yeah, uh-huh.

345
00:22:05,691 --> 00:22:06,957
Uh-huh, uh-huh, uh-huh.

346
00:22:06,992 --> 00:22:09,326
Uh-huh, yeah, okay, okay.

347
00:22:09,362 --> 00:22:10,728
Yeah. Bye.

348
00:22:10,763 --> 00:22:12,730
That was Mich-Michelle.

349
00:22:12,765 --> 00:22:14,665
So, uh...

350
00:22:14,700 --> 00:22:18,702
how often do you hear
from this, uh, Ferentol fella?

351
00:22:18,737 --> 00:22:20,270
Sundays.

352
00:22:30,349 --> 00:22:32,449
I think it'll work out.
Well, I'm just not

353
00:22:32,484 --> 00:22:34,129
feeling good about this...
New Image Cosmetics

354
00:22:34,153 --> 00:22:36,713
has never been in such
a compromising position.

355
00:22:38,090 --> 00:22:40,157
Oh. Oh, hi.

356
00:22:40,192 --> 00:22:43,461
Uh, I'm Ben Matlock,
Lauren Masters' lawyer.

357
00:22:43,496 --> 00:22:45,106
Mr. Anderson? Oh, uh...

358
00:22:45,130 --> 00:22:46,475
Mr. Anderson. I'm-I'm
sorry, Mr. Anderson,

359
00:22:46,499 --> 00:22:48,109
I couldn't stop
him. That's all right.

360
00:22:48,133 --> 00:22:50,211
What can I do for
you, Mr. Matlock? Well,

361
00:22:50,235 --> 00:22:52,147
I understand that
you're thinking

362
00:22:52,171 --> 00:22:54,771
of taking the "Reach
for the Stars" title

363
00:22:54,806 --> 00:22:56,039
away from Lauren.

364
00:22:56,074 --> 00:22:58,242
That's none of your
business, Mr. Matlock.

365
00:22:58,277 --> 00:22:59,277
Well, it-it is.

366
00:22:59,311 --> 00:23:01,378
See, you take that
title away from her,

367
00:23:01,413 --> 00:23:03,425
and it's the same
as saying she's guilty.

368
00:23:03,449 --> 00:23:05,594
The news media would
have her convicted

369
00:23:05,618 --> 00:23:07,496
before she ever goes to court.

370
00:23:07,520 --> 00:23:09,820
That's unfortunate, but
I can't permit scandals

371
00:23:09,855 --> 00:23:12,222
to tarnish the reputation
of New Image Cosmetics.

372
00:23:12,257 --> 00:23:13,590
Oh, no, no, no, no.

373
00:23:13,625 --> 00:23:15,559
But how about
this? How about this?

374
00:23:15,594 --> 00:23:17,060
You stand by Lauren.

375
00:23:17,095 --> 00:23:20,230
You say, "This is America.

376
00:23:20,265 --> 00:23:24,001
A person is innocent
until proven guilty."

377
00:23:24,036 --> 00:23:27,271
New Image would come
out smelling like a rose.

378
00:23:27,306 --> 00:23:28,850
I don't think that's
a very good idea.

379
00:23:28,874 --> 00:23:30,685
America would flock to
New Image. Mr. Matlock...

380
00:23:30,709 --> 00:23:32,776
Your profits would soar!

381
00:23:32,811 --> 00:23:34,244
What do you think?

382
00:23:34,279 --> 00:23:36,814
I like it, I do.

383
00:23:36,849 --> 00:23:39,249
Oh, but you can't...
Get DeFalco on it.

384
00:23:39,284 --> 00:23:40,844
Yeah.

385
00:23:43,121 --> 00:23:44,165
Thank you.

386
00:23:44,189 --> 00:23:48,158
Well, so these are
the, uh... contestants.

387
00:23:48,193 --> 00:23:49,826
Good-looking women there.

388
00:23:49,862 --> 00:23:51,072
These are the finalists.

389
00:23:51,096 --> 00:23:52,874
Each year I pick one of them

390
00:23:52,898 --> 00:23:56,733
to be my, uh, New Image
Cosmetics cover girl.

391
00:23:56,768 --> 00:23:58,647
I'd already decided
who the winner would be,

392
00:23:58,671 --> 00:24:00,782
and the next thing I
knew, she was murdered.

393
00:24:00,806 --> 00:24:04,141
Oh. You had chosen
Morgan Gerard.

394
00:24:05,744 --> 00:24:08,512
Did you tell anybody?

395
00:24:08,548 --> 00:24:10,747
I never got the chance.

396
00:24:10,782 --> 00:24:15,919
You know, there's a rumor
that Morgan was, uh...

397
00:24:15,954 --> 00:24:18,121
How do you say? <i>Seeing</i> somebody

398
00:24:18,157 --> 00:24:20,324
during the contest;

399
00:24:20,359 --> 00:24:23,126
somebody<i> involved</i>
in the contest.

400
00:24:23,162 --> 00:24:25,173
Mr. Matlock, that would
have been against the rules.

401
00:24:25,197 --> 00:24:28,999
You saying Morgan
Gerard wouldn't break rules?

402
00:24:29,035 --> 00:24:30,734
<i>I</i> never break the rules.

403
00:24:30,769 --> 00:24:34,805
Oh, oh. Well,
thanks for your help.

404
00:24:36,175 --> 00:24:38,709
And... oh, does New
Image make a aftershave?

405
00:24:38,744 --> 00:24:40,221
I'd like to kind
of get on board.

406
00:24:46,585 --> 00:24:49,252
Mr. Matlock, I just
want to apologize

407
00:24:49,288 --> 00:24:50,866
for coming on so strong.

408
00:24:50,890 --> 00:24:55,593
Oh, you had a point.
Not valid, but a point.

409
00:24:56,929 --> 00:24:58,674
I wouldn't do anything
to hurt Janet Masters.

410
00:24:58,698 --> 00:24:59,942
She's an old friend.

411
00:24:59,966 --> 00:25:01,843
And God knows she's been
through enough already.

412
00:25:01,867 --> 00:25:03,333
Oh, she has, hasn't she?

413
00:25:03,368 --> 00:25:04,668
I'm a friend, too.

414
00:25:04,704 --> 00:25:05,847
An old friend?

415
00:25:05,871 --> 00:25:07,671
Oh, yeah. I've known her

416
00:25:07,707 --> 00:25:09,006
since before she went to prison.

417
00:25:09,041 --> 00:25:10,273
You know about that?

418
00:25:10,309 --> 00:25:11,787
Oh, I've known her for 26 years.

419
00:25:11,811 --> 00:25:13,154
Of course I knew about that.

420
00:25:13,178 --> 00:25:16,413
I understand you were with
her the night of the party.

421
00:25:16,448 --> 00:25:17,547
What time did she leave?

422
00:25:17,583 --> 00:25:19,416
Oh, 11:15, 11:30.

423
00:25:32,598 --> 00:25:34,131
Oh!

424
00:25:34,166 --> 00:25:36,345
What a nice idea:
dinner at Templin's.

425
00:25:36,369 --> 00:25:37,369
Just like old times.

426
00:25:37,403 --> 00:25:39,814
Yes, you, the music,
even the pretzels.

427
00:25:39,838 --> 00:25:41,116
Yeah, yeah. Nothing's changed.

428
00:25:41,140 --> 00:25:43,274
Well, Ray Junior's on piano.

429
00:25:43,309 --> 00:25:44,309
Go get 'em, Ray!

430
00:25:44,343 --> 00:25:45,909
I got 'em!

431
00:25:47,880 --> 00:25:49,680
Look at these.

432
00:25:49,715 --> 00:25:55,919
Oh, you saved
all these pictures.

433
00:25:55,954 --> 00:25:57,288
Look at all of us.

434
00:25:57,323 --> 00:26:00,024
Those were great times for me.

435
00:26:00,059 --> 00:26:02,426
Was my hair ever that brown?

436
00:26:02,461 --> 00:26:03,471
Sure was.

437
00:26:03,495 --> 00:26:07,297
Damn that mule, right?

438
00:26:10,169 --> 00:26:12,903
How's it going, Ben? Have
you found out anything?

439
00:26:12,938 --> 00:26:16,806
Well, uh, I talked
with Don Mosher.

440
00:26:16,842 --> 00:26:19,076
You know... Well, of
course you know him.

441
00:26:19,111 --> 00:26:22,012
Uh... he said

442
00:26:22,047 --> 00:26:26,016
you left the party about 11:30.

443
00:26:26,051 --> 00:26:28,117
Yes, I did. My daughter
had just told me

444
00:26:28,153 --> 00:26:29,619
she was being blackmailed.

445
00:26:29,655 --> 00:26:32,022
I didn't feel like sticking
around and making small talk.

446
00:26:32,057 --> 00:26:35,625
Where'd you go?

447
00:26:35,660 --> 00:26:38,228
I went for a walk.
I needed some air.

448
00:26:38,263 --> 00:26:41,731
A girl was killed
between 11:30 and 12:00.

449
00:26:41,767 --> 00:26:45,936
I... I sure hope
somebody saw you.

450
00:26:48,540 --> 00:26:51,542
Oh, I don't believe this.

451
00:26:51,577 --> 00:26:53,477
Do you

452
00:26:53,512 --> 00:26:56,547
really think that I
murdered Morgan Gerard

453
00:26:56,582 --> 00:26:58,182
and let Lauren take the blame?

454
00:26:58,217 --> 00:27:01,151
Oh, no. Oh, no, no!

455
00:27:01,186 --> 00:27:04,088
Do you think that I would just
sit here and talk over old times

456
00:27:04,123 --> 00:27:05,601
with you while
Lauren went to prison?

457
00:27:05,625 --> 00:27:07,591
Oh, no, no, Janet, no!

458
00:27:07,626 --> 00:27:09,058
You go to hell.

459
00:27:28,313 --> 00:27:29,279
Hi.

460
00:27:29,314 --> 00:27:30,358
Hi.

461
00:27:30,382 --> 00:27:34,584
You've, uh, got some company.

462
00:27:34,619 --> 00:27:36,886
Mm? Mm-hmm.

463
00:27:47,733 --> 00:27:48,866
I am just so sorry

464
00:27:48,901 --> 00:27:50,300
about blowing up
at you last night?

465
00:27:50,335 --> 00:27:51,379
Oh, I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

466
00:27:51,403 --> 00:27:52,481
I had no reason...

467
00:27:52,505 --> 00:27:54,404
You had every right to
ask me those questions.

468
00:27:54,439 --> 00:27:55,650
I really had no reason.

469
00:27:55,674 --> 00:27:57,218
Let me just tell you something.

470
00:27:57,242 --> 00:27:58,954
I've been at this so long

471
00:27:58,978 --> 00:28:01,945
that I wake myself
up at night sometimes

472
00:28:01,981 --> 00:28:04,581
saying, "Where were you
at the time of the murder?

473
00:28:04,617 --> 00:28:06,795
"Can you corroborate
that? Was there a witness?

474
00:28:06,819 --> 00:28:08,329
Do you have an alibi?"

475
00:28:08,353 --> 00:28:10,353
Do you ever answer yourself?

476
00:28:10,389 --> 00:28:12,949
Sometimes. Let's
go have some coffee.

477
00:28:17,529 --> 00:28:18,928
I'm telling you I got an angle.

478
00:28:18,964 --> 00:28:20,964
I can double your bookings.

479
00:28:22,300 --> 00:28:24,168
Hey, listen, I gotta go.

480
00:28:24,203 --> 00:28:26,837
No, no, no, you
think about it, okay?

481
00:28:26,872 --> 00:28:28,872
What can I do for
you, sweetheart?

482
00:28:28,907 --> 00:28:31,308
Uh, Michelle Thomas.

483
00:28:31,343 --> 00:28:35,479
Michelle. That's
good. Have a seat.

484
00:28:35,514 --> 00:28:37,147
So what are you into, Michelle?

485
00:28:37,182 --> 00:28:40,150
Singing, acting, modeling, what?

486
00:28:40,185 --> 00:28:42,218
Uh, answers.

487
00:28:42,254 --> 00:28:43,286
Mm-hmm.

488
00:28:43,321 --> 00:28:46,289
I'm an attorney
for Lauren Masters.

489
00:28:46,324 --> 00:28:47,457
Attorney?

490
00:28:47,492 --> 00:28:50,727
What a waste of what you got.

491
00:28:50,763 --> 00:28:52,674
Um, what is all this?

492
00:28:52,698 --> 00:28:54,831
I thought you were
working for Don Mosher.

493
00:28:54,866 --> 00:28:56,032
No, Mosher's a dinosaur.

494
00:28:56,067 --> 00:28:58,135
As soon as I set up
my agency, I'm gone.

495
00:28:58,170 --> 00:28:59,136
Well, I bet you met

496
00:28:59,171 --> 00:29:00,282
a lot of potential clients

497
00:29:00,306 --> 00:29:02,639
setting up Reach
For The Stars for him.

498
00:29:02,674 --> 00:29:04,407
That was the idea.

499
00:29:04,443 --> 00:29:07,778
Were you gonna
sign Morgan Gerard?

500
00:29:07,813 --> 00:29:08,912
Maybe.

501
00:29:08,947 --> 00:29:10,947
Is that why you were
sleeping with her?

502
00:29:15,020 --> 00:29:16,253
Who told you that?

503
00:29:16,288 --> 00:29:20,057
See, you forgot to be
nice to the little people.

504
00:29:20,092 --> 00:29:23,359
Or at least to make sure that
when you pay someone off

505
00:29:23,395 --> 00:29:25,562
not to talk, the
check doesn't bounce.

506
00:29:25,597 --> 00:29:30,601
Whoever the
creep is, he's lying.

507
00:29:30,636 --> 00:29:33,937
Well, that's why
we have courts...

508
00:29:33,972 --> 00:29:37,240
To figure out who's
lying and who isn't.

509
00:29:37,275 --> 00:29:39,509
See you there.

510
00:29:50,155 --> 00:29:52,367
Ben, I want you to know

511
00:29:52,391 --> 00:29:54,503
I've asked to be
reassigned from the case.

512
00:29:54,527 --> 00:29:56,226
Reassigned? Why?

513
00:29:56,261 --> 00:29:58,339
I just think this is
one of those times

514
00:29:58,363 --> 00:30:01,097
when our professional
rivalry might damage

515
00:30:01,133 --> 00:30:02,744
our personal relationship.

516
00:30:02,768 --> 00:30:05,201
Oh, well... It's my call.

517
00:30:05,237 --> 00:30:09,205
Well, who's, uh,
who's replacing you?

518
00:30:09,241 --> 00:30:10,485
Dave Hawkins.

519
00:30:10,509 --> 00:30:13,109
Dave Hawkins?

520
00:30:13,145 --> 00:30:16,646
You're having Hangman
Hawkins replace you?

521
00:30:16,681 --> 00:30:19,049
You think he's
tougher than I am?

522
00:30:19,084 --> 00:30:21,418
Oh, uh... Ben, you called

523
00:30:21,453 --> 00:30:23,487
him "Hangman Hawkins."

524
00:30:23,522 --> 00:30:25,500
Well, yeah. Do you ever
call me names like that?

525
00:30:25,524 --> 00:30:27,969
I call you lots of names behind
your back. I've never heard you.

526
00:30:27,993 --> 00:30:29,070
Well, I've never heard you.

527
00:30:29,094 --> 00:30:30,894
I'm not gonna go right up to

528
00:30:30,929 --> 00:30:33,596
Dave Hawkins and say, "What
say, Hangman? How's tricks?"

529
00:30:33,631 --> 00:30:35,598
Just fine, Ben. See you inside.

530
00:30:43,241 --> 00:30:46,443
Prosecution calls Mrs.
Janet Masters to the stand.

531
00:30:59,691 --> 00:31:01,925
21 years ago, you
were convicted of fraud.

532
00:31:01,960 --> 00:31:04,594
You served eight
months in prison.

533
00:31:04,629 --> 00:31:05,595
Is that correct?

534
00:31:05,630 --> 00:31:09,733
Well, you see, my
husband... Yes or no.

535
00:31:09,768 --> 00:31:10,901
Yes.

536
00:31:10,936 --> 00:31:12,947
Now you own and run
a public relations firm

537
00:31:12,971 --> 00:31:14,070
in New York City.

538
00:31:14,106 --> 00:31:16,740
According to this
profit and loss report,

539
00:31:16,775 --> 00:31:19,576
you made a very nice
profit last year, didn't you?

540
00:31:19,611 --> 00:31:20,677
Yes, we did.

541
00:31:20,712 --> 00:31:22,357
Before the murder
of Morgan Gerard,

542
00:31:22,381 --> 00:31:24,314
and the subsequent publicity,

543
00:31:24,349 --> 00:31:27,083
how many of your clients
knew that you'd been in prison?

544
00:31:27,119 --> 00:31:28,251
None.

545
00:31:28,286 --> 00:31:29,319
How many know now?

546
00:31:29,354 --> 00:31:30,320
I have no idea.

547
00:31:30,355 --> 00:31:32,455
How many clients have you lost

548
00:31:32,490 --> 00:31:34,269
because of the disclosure
of your prison record?

549
00:31:34,293 --> 00:31:35,992
I object. None of this

550
00:31:36,027 --> 00:31:39,829
has anything whatsoever to do with
the innocence or guilt of my client.

551
00:31:39,864 --> 00:31:41,397
It goes to motive, Your Honor.

552
00:31:41,433 --> 00:31:43,567
This witness is the
defendant's mother.

553
00:31:43,602 --> 00:31:44,879
What affects her
affects the defendant.

554
00:31:44,903 --> 00:31:46,436
Overruled.

555
00:31:46,471 --> 00:31:48,638
How many clients have
you lost, Mrs. Masters?

556
00:31:48,673 --> 00:31:49,939
I'm not sure.

557
00:31:49,975 --> 00:31:52,008
Well, four, five?

558
00:31:52,043 --> 00:31:53,610
Six?

559
00:31:54,980 --> 00:31:56,780
Your Honor?

560
00:31:56,815 --> 00:31:58,726
The witness will
answer the question.

561
00:31:58,750 --> 00:32:01,351
Eight. Eight.

562
00:32:01,386 --> 00:32:03,820
You're not gonna be in
the black this year, are you,

563
00:32:03,855 --> 00:32:05,166
Mrs. Masters? No.

564
00:32:05,190 --> 00:32:07,301
And that's why you kept
your prison record a secret,

565
00:32:07,325 --> 00:32:09,003
because you knew your clients
would leave you, didn't you?

566
00:32:09,027 --> 00:32:12,262
Yes or no, Mrs. Masters?

567
00:32:12,297 --> 00:32:13,430
Yes.

568
00:32:13,465 --> 00:32:15,465
And Lauren knew
this, too, didn't she?

569
00:32:18,036 --> 00:32:19,469
But she didn't...!

570
00:32:19,504 --> 00:32:20,937
Yes or no?

571
00:32:20,973 --> 00:32:22,406
Yes!

572
00:32:22,441 --> 00:32:24,152
Which is why she went
up to Morgan Gerard's room

573
00:32:24,176 --> 00:32:25,042
that night and murdered her!

574
00:32:25,077 --> 00:32:27,210
Objection! Objection!

575
00:32:27,245 --> 00:32:28,444
She did no such thing!

576
00:32:28,480 --> 00:32:29,891
I'll withdraw it, Your Honor.

577
00:32:29,915 --> 00:32:32,949
Nothing further, Your Honor.

578
00:32:42,093 --> 00:32:44,026
Oh, Janet feels terrible
about her testimony.

579
00:32:44,062 --> 00:32:46,107
Oh, she did the best she could.

580
00:32:46,131 --> 00:32:49,432
That Hangman
Hawkins is really good.

581
00:32:49,468 --> 00:32:54,671
Yeah. Well, anyway, here's
the credit check on Joey DeFalco.

582
00:32:54,706 --> 00:32:55,938
He owes everybody:

583
00:32:55,974 --> 00:32:58,908
clothing stores,
landlord, phone company.

584
00:32:58,943 --> 00:33:02,813
He used to drive a red
Corvette. Repossessed.

585
00:33:02,848 --> 00:33:07,650
Mm. You suppose he was using
Morgan Gerard to stay afloat?

586
00:33:07,685 --> 00:33:10,554
I'm sure he'd use anybody.

587
00:33:10,589 --> 00:33:14,257
How do you think Morgan knew

588
00:33:14,292 --> 00:33:15,992
about Janet's prison record?

589
00:33:16,027 --> 00:33:17,828
I mean, very few people.

590
00:33:17,863 --> 00:33:19,673
Oh, I don't know, I don't know.

591
00:33:19,697 --> 00:33:21,475
She couldn't have
just stumbled onto it.

592
00:33:21,499 --> 00:33:24,968
Somebody had to have told
her or she found some kind of...

593
00:33:29,541 --> 00:33:33,009
Now, when you first met
Janet Masters and were told

594
00:33:33,044 --> 00:33:35,278
that she was the first

595
00:33:35,313 --> 00:33:40,350
Reach For The Stars
contest winner 26 years ago,

596
00:33:40,385 --> 00:33:41,385
what did you do?

597
00:33:41,420 --> 00:33:43,620
What do you mean, what did I do?

598
00:33:43,655 --> 00:33:45,956
Well, you didn't see this
mother-and-daughter angle

599
00:33:45,991 --> 00:33:49,126
as something you could
exploit in the media?

600
00:33:49,161 --> 00:33:50,460
I recognize that.

601
00:33:50,496 --> 00:33:52,240
Yeah. Well, what
did you do about that?

602
00:33:52,264 --> 00:33:54,731
Nothing. I didn't know
if Lauren would win.

603
00:33:54,766 --> 00:33:57,867
You went ahead and
prepared a press kit, didn't you?

604
00:33:57,902 --> 00:33:59,847
Yes, I prepared a
press kit. Mm-hmm.

605
00:33:59,871 --> 00:34:03,273
And, and you went to where
Don Mosher keeps his files

606
00:34:03,308 --> 00:34:07,544
on his contest winners,
and you, you took Janet's file.

607
00:34:07,579 --> 00:34:09,513
No.

608
00:34:09,548 --> 00:34:10,624
Are you sure?

609
00:34:10,648 --> 00:34:13,149
Because, uh, uh,
her file is missing,

610
00:34:13,184 --> 00:34:17,888
and of all 26 files, hers is
the only one that's missing.

611
00:34:17,923 --> 00:34:19,456
You sure you don't have it?

612
00:34:19,491 --> 00:34:22,926
It'd be very embarrassing
if the police got a warrant

613
00:34:22,961 --> 00:34:25,362
and found that you did.

614
00:34:25,397 --> 00:34:28,965
Now hold on. I, uh,
I remember now.

615
00:34:29,001 --> 00:34:30,812
I think I do have
that file. Yeah.

616
00:34:30,836 --> 00:34:33,470
That's right. I took it
so I could go over it.

617
00:34:33,505 --> 00:34:35,872
Go over it. Yeah, sure,
sure. So what was in it?

618
00:34:35,907 --> 00:34:38,475
Some old photos, Don's notes.

619
00:34:38,510 --> 00:34:41,878
Mm-hmm. Were there
any press clippings?

620
00:34:41,913 --> 00:34:43,346
Don't remember.

621
00:34:43,381 --> 00:34:48,418
If I told you that Don Mosher
specifically remembers

622
00:34:48,453 --> 00:34:52,689
putting clippings
about Janet's conviction

623
00:34:52,724 --> 00:34:56,059
in her file, would that
refresh your memory any?

624
00:34:56,094 --> 00:34:57,927
Okay, so I saw them.

625
00:34:57,962 --> 00:34:59,107
Saw it.

626
00:34:59,131 --> 00:35:00,131
Yeah, yeah.

627
00:35:00,165 --> 00:35:01,743
Yeah, who did you
tell about them?

628
00:35:01,767 --> 00:35:02,732
Nobody.

629
00:35:02,768 --> 00:35:04,212
Not even Morgan Gerard?

630
00:35:04,236 --> 00:35:06,136
Why would I do that?

631
00:35:06,171 --> 00:35:12,008
Well, I understand you
want to be a talent agent.

632
00:35:12,044 --> 00:35:14,143
Yeah. No big secret.

633
00:35:14,179 --> 00:35:16,746
Especially for young
girls... Young, pretty girls.

634
00:35:16,782 --> 00:35:18,815
What can I say? I like girls.

635
00:35:18,850 --> 00:35:20,528
I see.

636
00:35:20,552 --> 00:35:22,018
I also understand

637
00:35:22,053 --> 00:35:25,421
that you're pretty heavy
in debt all over town.

638
00:35:25,457 --> 00:35:26,756
So?

639
00:35:26,791 --> 00:35:28,169
So, you were counting on

640
00:35:28,193 --> 00:35:30,560
Morgan winning that contest,

641
00:35:30,595 --> 00:35:34,264
signing with you as
your first big client

642
00:35:34,299 --> 00:35:35,510
and getting you
out of debt, right?

643
00:35:35,534 --> 00:35:37,267
She was gonna sign with me.

644
00:35:37,302 --> 00:35:39,147
From watching rehearsals,

645
00:35:39,171 --> 00:35:43,339
you knew if anybody was gonna
beat Morgan, it would be Lauren,

646
00:35:43,374 --> 00:35:46,776
so you told Morgan
about Janet's past.

647
00:35:46,812 --> 00:35:49,312
So, if Lauren did win,

648
00:35:49,347 --> 00:35:52,749
Morgan could
blackmail her into losing.

649
00:35:52,784 --> 00:35:54,517
And it worked.

650
00:35:54,552 --> 00:35:58,054
Except Morgan
double-crossed you, didn't she?

651
00:35:58,090 --> 00:36:00,056
I don't know what
you're talking about.

652
00:36:00,092 --> 00:36:02,652
Yes, you do. Yes, you do.

653
00:36:03,995 --> 00:36:10,299
She signed with TLM
Talent Agency in Los Angeles,

654
00:36:10,335 --> 00:36:12,602
didn't she?

655
00:36:12,637 --> 00:36:14,715
And you found out
about it at the party.

656
00:36:14,739 --> 00:36:16,339
I heard about it.

657
00:36:16,375 --> 00:36:19,643
Yeah. I guess it
made you pretty mad.

658
00:36:19,678 --> 00:36:20,810
It made me mad, yes.

659
00:36:20,845 --> 00:36:22,190
Mm-hmm. You know,

660
00:36:22,214 --> 00:36:25,281
Nobody remembers seeing
you at the party after 11:30.

661
00:36:25,317 --> 00:36:26,449
Where did you go?

662
00:36:26,484 --> 00:36:28,151
That's my business.

663
00:36:28,186 --> 00:36:30,319
You went up to Morgan's
room, didn't you?

664
00:36:30,355 --> 00:36:31,988
Nope. And you killed her.

665
00:36:32,023 --> 00:36:33,623
No, I did not.

666
00:36:33,658 --> 00:36:36,492
Where did you go, Mr. DeFalco?

667
00:36:39,898 --> 00:36:41,364
Oh, hell, why not?

668
00:36:41,399 --> 00:36:44,701
I was in... Dana Williams' room.

669
00:36:44,736 --> 00:36:48,405
We were engaged in... uh...

670
00:36:48,440 --> 00:36:51,775
pre-contractual negotiations.

671
00:36:55,180 --> 00:36:57,280
Hey! I'm sorry, baby.

672
00:37:06,091 --> 00:37:08,024
Nothing further.

673
00:37:20,138 --> 00:37:22,439
Ben!

674
00:37:22,474 --> 00:37:23,606
Wait!

675
00:37:23,641 --> 00:37:25,208
Oh, hi, Julie.

676
00:37:25,243 --> 00:37:27,743
I hear it didn't go
very well in there.

677
00:37:27,779 --> 00:37:32,782
Well, Hangman Hawkins
ain't singing the blues.

678
00:37:32,817 --> 00:37:34,917
Come on. Lunch is on me.

679
00:37:34,953 --> 00:37:36,886
Okay.

680
00:37:39,891 --> 00:37:43,659
Hey.

681
00:37:43,695 --> 00:37:45,228
What will it be?

682
00:37:45,263 --> 00:37:49,632
Steak, barbecue, or how
about a nice grilled trout?

683
00:37:49,667 --> 00:37:51,867
Ah...

684
00:38:03,347 --> 00:38:05,760
Everybody and his brother
has been over this room.

685
00:38:05,784 --> 00:38:09,385
Well... Well, we might
as well do it again.

686
00:38:09,421 --> 00:38:10,653
You know what the song says.

687
00:38:10,688 --> 00:38:13,248
Everything's better
the second time around.

688
00:38:15,160 --> 00:38:17,627
This is New Image
Cosmetics' entire line.

689
00:38:17,662 --> 00:38:19,296
Yeah.

690
00:38:19,331 --> 00:38:22,865
Uh, there's three
fingernails missing from this...

691
00:38:22,901 --> 00:38:24,267
line right here.

692
00:38:24,303 --> 00:38:25,702
They're hard to put on?

693
00:38:25,737 --> 00:38:27,548
Well, the hardest part is
putting them on straight.

694
00:38:27,572 --> 00:38:31,074
Huh... Can you get me those

695
00:38:31,109 --> 00:38:33,669
autopsy pictures, will you?

696
00:38:43,588 --> 00:38:46,556
<i>Uh, now, your company,</i>

697
00:38:46,591 --> 00:38:49,959
New Image Cosmetics,
has sponsored

698
00:38:49,994 --> 00:38:53,596
the Reach for the Stars
contest for-for how long?

699
00:38:53,631 --> 00:38:55,732
Seven years. Seven years.

700
00:38:55,767 --> 00:38:58,535
And how long have
you known Joe DeFalco?

701
00:38:58,570 --> 00:39:00,547
He came aboard two years ago.

702
00:39:00,571 --> 00:39:01,705
Do you know him well?

703
00:39:01,740 --> 00:39:04,574
We're not friends.

704
00:39:04,609 --> 00:39:07,877
Well, why would you
give him $45,000?

705
00:39:07,912 --> 00:39:10,346
What makes you think I did that?

706
00:39:11,549 --> 00:39:13,016
He told me you did.

707
00:39:13,051 --> 00:39:15,352
I asked him

708
00:39:15,387 --> 00:39:18,688
how he got back his
repossessed sports car,

709
00:39:18,723 --> 00:39:20,957
and he told me
that he told you that

710
00:39:20,992 --> 00:39:23,126
if you didn't give him $45,000,

711
00:39:23,161 --> 00:39:26,062
he was going to tell the police
about you and Morgan Gerard.

712
00:39:27,432 --> 00:39:29,299
Joey is a special
kind of dude, isn't he?

713
00:39:29,334 --> 00:39:33,069
Took about five
minutes for him to tell me.

714
00:39:33,104 --> 00:39:35,271
Joey's the one who
introduced you to Morgan

715
00:39:35,306 --> 00:39:37,251
when she was competing
in Nashville, isn't he?

716
00:39:37,275 --> 00:39:38,641
Oh, yes, but...

717
00:39:38,677 --> 00:39:41,911
Is-is-is that when your
affair with her started?

718
00:39:41,947 --> 00:39:43,846
No.

719
00:39:43,882 --> 00:39:45,448
Oh, come on.

720
00:39:45,483 --> 00:39:49,151
And it wasn't Joey that
she was seeing on the sly

721
00:39:49,187 --> 00:39:51,588
during the competition
here in Atlanta.

722
00:39:51,623 --> 00:39:53,156
It was you, wasn't it?

723
00:39:53,191 --> 00:39:54,423
No!

724
00:39:54,459 --> 00:39:56,292
And it was because
of your affair

725
00:39:56,327 --> 00:40:00,062
with her that you made her
the new Image Cover girl.

726
00:40:00,098 --> 00:40:01,231
Right?

727
00:40:01,266 --> 00:40:03,366
No, there was no
personal relationship.

728
00:40:03,401 --> 00:40:06,769
Oh, I know there was
no personal relationship.

729
00:40:06,804 --> 00:40:08,771
There was no care.

730
00:40:08,806 --> 00:40:12,308
There was no real love.

731
00:40:12,343 --> 00:40:16,112
I imagine, at times,
your relationship got...

732
00:40:16,147 --> 00:40:20,883
How'd you call...
pretty intense,

733
00:40:20,919 --> 00:40:24,620
till you found out that
she was just using you.

734
00:40:24,656 --> 00:40:26,155
She didn't want you,

735
00:40:26,190 --> 00:40:31,594
just you, she wanted to
be the New Image cover girl.

736
00:40:32,397 --> 00:40:34,164
She wanted a lot of things,

737
00:40:34,199 --> 00:40:36,199
and she would do anything

738
00:40:36,234 --> 00:40:38,468
she had to to get them.

739
00:40:44,009 --> 00:40:46,554
She spent some time with
Joey. Did you know that?

740
00:40:48,713 --> 00:40:50,880
Over the years, there were a lot

741
00:40:50,915 --> 00:40:56,119
of beautiful New
Image cover girls.

742
00:40:56,154 --> 00:40:58,654
But Morgan...

743
00:40:58,689 --> 00:41:03,859
she was the only one, the
only one that you fell in...

744
00:41:03,895 --> 00:41:05,928
How'd you call that?

745
00:41:05,963 --> 00:41:11,134
That wonderful
middle-aged love with.

746
00:41:12,904 --> 00:41:15,071
She's the one that
made a fool out of you.

747
00:41:15,106 --> 00:41:16,638
No! Objection!

748
00:41:16,674 --> 00:41:19,075
Counsel's badgering the witness.

749
00:41:19,110 --> 00:41:21,377
He's trying to pass
off his wild speculation

750
00:41:21,412 --> 00:41:22,845
as questions.

751
00:41:22,880 --> 00:41:24,525
Mr. Matlock, I don't
feel entirely comfortable

752
00:41:24,549 --> 00:41:26,582
about this line of
questioning, either.

753
00:41:26,617 --> 00:41:28,517
Uh, Your Honor, I
have to level with you.

754
00:41:28,553 --> 00:41:30,286
I don't feel
comfortable, myself.

755
00:41:31,422 --> 00:41:36,359
Uh, would you mind
telling us what this is?

756
00:41:36,394 --> 00:41:39,662
That's an artificial fingernail
kit put out by my company.

757
00:41:39,697 --> 00:41:41,664
Uh-huh. And how does it work?

758
00:41:41,700 --> 00:41:43,032
You just, uh...

759
00:41:43,068 --> 00:41:47,336
You peel this little thing off
here and then just stick it on?

760
00:41:47,371 --> 00:41:51,908
Uh, yes, there is glue on the
adhesive backing for each nail.

761
00:41:51,943 --> 00:41:54,243
I see. Now, this was found

762
00:41:56,013 --> 00:41:59,749
In Morgan Gerard's room,
so I guess we can assume

763
00:41:59,784 --> 00:42:03,653
that she was wearing
these false fingernails

764
00:42:03,688 --> 00:42:06,422
when she was killed, and
they came from this kit.

765
00:42:06,457 --> 00:42:08,391
That make sense?

766
00:42:08,426 --> 00:42:09,893
I suppose so.

767
00:42:09,928 --> 00:42:13,429
Now, how many, how many
nails come in these kits?

768
00:42:13,464 --> 00:42:14,708
20, two complete sets.

769
00:42:14,732 --> 00:42:15,865
Twenty.

770
00:42:15,901 --> 00:42:17,867
Now, there are 13 missing.

771
00:42:17,903 --> 00:42:19,869
These and these...

772
00:42:19,904 --> 00:42:22,271
These three right
here. Why would she

773
00:42:22,307 --> 00:42:23,939
replace just three nails?

774
00:42:25,777 --> 00:42:29,879
Well, they could chip or
break off or even fall off

775
00:42:29,914 --> 00:42:31,314
if they're not properly applied.

776
00:42:31,349 --> 00:42:32,493
Well, I thought
all you had to do

777
00:42:32,517 --> 00:42:34,028
was just stick it on, like that.

778
00:42:34,052 --> 00:42:37,686
Well, you have to hold it in
place for at least ten seconds

779
00:42:37,722 --> 00:42:40,256
to allow the, uh, glue
to bond to the nail.

780
00:42:40,291 --> 00:42:41,591
Uh-huh.

781
00:42:41,626 --> 00:42:43,693
Now, let me show you this.

782
00:42:45,663 --> 00:42:52,702
This is a part of the
People's Exhibit 15.

783
00:42:53,771 --> 00:42:55,605
It's an autopsy photograph.

784
00:42:55,640 --> 00:42:58,073
This is the
decedent's right hand.

785
00:42:58,109 --> 00:43:00,075
Now, would you
just take a look at that

786
00:43:00,111 --> 00:43:02,945
and describe these nails to us.

787
00:43:05,750 --> 00:43:08,095
Looks like some of the
fingernails are on crooked. Yeah.

788
00:43:08,119 --> 00:43:11,787
These three right here.

789
00:43:11,822 --> 00:43:13,822
The coroner told me

790
00:43:13,858 --> 00:43:16,192
that when they were
scraping under these nails...

791
00:43:16,227 --> 00:43:19,195
You know, for
bits of skin, hair...

792
00:43:19,230 --> 00:43:23,166
These three nails right
here just fell right off.

793
00:43:23,201 --> 00:43:26,402
And he put them
back the best he could,

794
00:43:26,438 --> 00:43:29,072
but why would these
three just fall right off?

795
00:43:29,107 --> 00:43:30,206
Objection, Your Honor.

796
00:43:30,241 --> 00:43:31,952
Overruled. Oh, I'm
sorry, Your Honor.

797
00:43:31,976 --> 00:43:33,642
Mr. Matlock, I'll be the judge.

798
00:43:33,678 --> 00:43:34,877
Overruled.

799
00:43:34,913 --> 00:43:36,646
Answer the question.

800
00:43:36,681 --> 00:43:37,780
Yes.

801
00:43:39,150 --> 00:43:42,952
I... Well, they were put
on improperly, I suppose.

802
00:43:42,987 --> 00:43:46,488
Or maybe the person
who put them on,

803
00:43:46,524 --> 00:43:49,158
put them on very hastily

804
00:43:49,193 --> 00:43:53,562
and didn't have time
for the glue to hold.

805
00:43:53,597 --> 00:43:55,064
Maybe the killer.

806
00:43:55,099 --> 00:43:57,133
How would I know that?

807
00:43:57,168 --> 00:44:00,069
When Morgan Gerard
double-crossed Joey DeFalco,

808
00:44:00,105 --> 00:44:03,873
then he double-crossed
her by telling you

809
00:44:03,908 --> 00:44:06,475
that she'd been
sleeping around on you.

810
00:44:06,511 --> 00:44:10,913
And I imagine a fellow like you,
that would make you pretty hot.

811
00:44:10,949 --> 00:44:13,182
You went up to her room
that night, didn't you?

812
00:44:13,218 --> 00:44:15,351
No, I didn't. Of
course, you did.

813
00:44:15,386 --> 00:44:17,298
And you confronted her
with what Joey had told you.

814
00:44:17,322 --> 00:44:19,655
You know, about sleeping
on the wrong side of the bed.

815
00:44:19,690 --> 00:44:22,959
And maybe she
said, "Yes, I have."

816
00:44:22,994 --> 00:44:25,228
Or maybe she said,
"What's it to you, old man?"

817
00:44:25,263 --> 00:44:26,863
Or maybe she said, "Go to hell.

818
00:44:26,898 --> 00:44:28,542
How about it?" How
about you going to hell?

819
00:44:28,566 --> 00:44:30,032
And during your lovers' quarrel,

820
00:44:30,067 --> 00:44:31,412
you bludgeoned her,
but she fought back.

821
00:44:31,436 --> 00:44:33,102
She lashed out at you,

822
00:44:33,137 --> 00:44:36,038
and that's how she broke
those nails, clawing at your skin.

823
00:44:36,073 --> 00:44:37,639
Your Honor!

824
00:44:37,675 --> 00:44:38,808
And you saw the nails

825
00:44:38,843 --> 00:44:40,643
on the floor. You
picked them up,

826
00:44:40,678 --> 00:44:42,478
put them in your pocket, quick.

827
00:44:42,513 --> 00:44:44,580
You knew your skin was on them.

828
00:44:44,615 --> 00:44:46,816
And you replaced them
with these three, didn't you?

829
00:44:46,851 --> 00:44:48,751
You can't prove this!

830
00:44:48,786 --> 00:44:50,030
Just pull down your
turtleneck sweater.

831
00:44:50,054 --> 00:44:51,187
What?

832
00:44:51,222 --> 00:44:53,322
Pull down your sweater
a little bit, so we can see

833
00:44:53,357 --> 00:44:55,958
the gouges Morgan made,

834
00:44:55,993 --> 00:44:58,061
clawing at you. I
don't have any gouges.

835
00:44:58,096 --> 00:44:59,239
Pull it down. Just pull it

836
00:44:59,263 --> 00:45:01,764
just a little. Get out of here.

837
00:45:04,035 --> 00:45:07,470
Okay. Okay, but I'll tell you.

838
00:45:07,505 --> 00:45:12,008
When the judge or
three or four cops

839
00:45:12,043 --> 00:45:13,520
want you to pull
down that sweater,

840
00:45:13,544 --> 00:45:16,312
you're going to pull
down that sweater.

841
00:45:19,250 --> 00:45:21,684
Reasonable doubt,
Your Honor, for my client.

842
00:45:21,719 --> 00:45:25,655
That's all I have to
prove, Mr. Anderson.

843
00:45:25,690 --> 00:45:27,623
Reasonable doubt.

844
00:45:39,604 --> 00:45:42,405
We, the jury, find the
defendant not guilty.

845
00:45:42,440 --> 00:45:46,008
Not guilty verdict is
entered into the record.

846
00:45:46,043 --> 00:45:47,376
This court is adjourned.

847
00:46:00,758 --> 00:46:02,825
Well, here we are.

848
00:46:02,860 --> 00:46:03,970
I'm so happy.

849
00:46:03,994 --> 00:46:05,361
Oh, so am I.

850
00:46:05,396 --> 00:46:07,675
I'll never forget
this, Ben, never.

851
00:46:07,699 --> 00:46:09,532
There's a lot of
things I won't forget.

852
00:46:09,567 --> 00:46:11,834
Ben, you did a great job.

853
00:46:11,869 --> 00:46:13,013
Hi, Julie.

854
00:46:13,037 --> 00:46:14,870
You must be very relieved.

855
00:46:14,906 --> 00:46:16,083
We both are.

856
00:46:16,107 --> 00:46:17,373
We're anxious to get home.

857
00:46:17,408 --> 00:46:19,008
You're leaving right away?

858
00:46:19,043 --> 00:46:20,187
Oh, first thing in the morning,

859
00:46:20,211 --> 00:46:21,955
as soon as we're packed.

860
00:46:21,979 --> 00:46:23,312
Oh.

861
00:46:28,352 --> 00:46:33,789
So, tell me, what names do
you call me behind my back?

862
00:46:37,228 --> 00:46:39,161
Honey.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
